<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan sells 30,000 tns Oct fuel oil near $116/tn.</title>
<headline>Taiwan sells 30,000 tns Oct fuel oil near $116/tn.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) sold by tender a 30,000-tonne cargo of high sulphur fuel oil at nearly $116 per tonne on a free-on-board basis, a CPC source said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The 180-centistoke grade fuel oil with a 3.0-percent sulphur content will be lifted from Kaohsiung between October 1 and 10, the source said.</p>
<p>The tender closed on September 16.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65-870-3082)</p>
